{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551134-new-players-help","id":1551134,"title":"New Players (help)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-18T20:22:27-07:00","id":1551134,"title":"New Players (help)","content":"So I will be hosting a game (maybe a campaign) for some new players. They know next to nothing about Vampire. Looking for some ideas how to approach this.<br /> I have had new players before but never a whole group of players.<br /> I'd like to avoid doing a bunch single sessions. <br /> Any ideas would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-18T23:41:36-07:00","id":1551135,"title":"","content":"I think the best would be to sit down with them and spend an hour or so to explain them the World of Darkess/Vampire, the setting with broad strokes eg. this is like our world just there are monsters and you are one of them, Clans, Sects, ruling body and so on<br /> Map out a bit what they want - after all, at the end of the day it is all about having fun - trenchcoat and katanas, political powerplays, war-torn city (under siege, Sabbat, Anarch, etc, ) and combat oriented or social Elyisum parties, missions from the Prince as his unoffical &quot;hands&quot; (aka. Suicide Squad) and/or slow entanglement in the web of the Ancients<br /> It helps if you know if they want to explore the soulwrenching personal horror is to be a vempire, the slow withering of Humanity, driwfting away who they were and realizing what they slowly become... or blood fueled &quot;superheroes&quot; with cool powers with a passing mention, oh, I ate a few kids along the way<br /> There is no &quot;Play the game Wrong&quot;!<br /> If everyone is a new player then maybe worth to spend everyone a single session to play out the last few days of their Human Lives as Mortals and their Embrace and the following few nights as a fledgeling then herd them together a Teen Titans like fashion; the Prince cashed in a few favors to form a team of fresh Vampires for whatever reason from a My Fair Lady-like bet with another Prince/Ancient (in my City old chap, even the fledglings are high quality and could become valuable members! Bonus points if the other Prince/Ancient works hard to sabotage them... or they have to sabotage the other team) to the those Sires managed to piss of the Ruler and the Prince allowed the Embrace, bid his time to make them look bad by making their kid's life Hell; he gives them tasks but expect them to fail and so on. The Sabbat (or whataver you want) howls at the gates and we need fresh soldiers commandante (it especially fun when they ran in the enemy who are just &quot;kids&quot; like them - we are not so different, you and I - or even befriend them before both sides realizes oh shit, they are the bad guys. Wait, we are the baddies???)<br /> At the end of the day I think the most important to know what they want to play and structure your stories around them, after all ,they are the stars of the show","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-19-2025, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T09:03:07-07:00","id":1551138,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1551134-new-players-help?p=1551135#post1551135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps if you know if they want to explore the soulwrenching personal horror is to be a vempire, the slow withering of Humanity, driwfting away who they were and realizing what they slowly become... or blood fueled &quot;superheroes&quot; with cool powers with a passing mention, oh, I ate a few kids along the way...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I feel is most important for them. I mean, if you just give them a few options, things to keep in mind as they go? They won't think of it all as a decisions that need to be made in Session Zero. Rather, I'd suggest making it a conversation that keeps coming up. My troupe has been playing the same chronicle for over twenty years, and we STILL have these conversations from time to time.<br /> <br /> In terms of rules and setting, allowing for exploration helps keep anyone from feeling either railroaded or trapped \u2014 ideally they won't feel any of this, of course \u2014 with choices they made early on. Like, if you allow them to choose a clan and whatnot, keep them to it. However, I told my players that most of their backgrounds (lower case AND the traits), Abilities, etc. were up for editing through play. It allowed them a bit more freedom.<br /> <br /> The biggest bit of advice I'd give for YOU is that you'll want to remain flexible, curious, and open in your approach with new players. That does not mean letting them get away with anything. It means allowing them to figure it out on their own without being an antagonist. You can model behavior that you want them to exhibit. </span>Don't rely on individual sessions if they will pay attention to each others' origins. If the players see what the others are doing, see how you approach each of their characters and the choices made for said characters, it will build trust. Trust is the best tool you, as a Storyteller, have whether it is for new or well-established players.<br /> <br /> Finally, make sure it is fun. That sounds silly and too-easy as pointers go, but you don't want to get so bogged down in setting and rules and what-this-monster-did-to-that-monster-in-the-year-of-our-lord-1022 that it pickles anyone's brain. There's time for that, and if things look like they're getting dull, feel free to change the approach. I reckon this goes along with the above 'flexible, curious, and open.' If you make sure they are having fun and YOU are having fun, there's nothing that will wreck it. <br /> <br /> ...I'm kind of jealous of you getting to introduce the game to newbies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-19T09:33:26-07:00","id":1551139,"title":"","content":"I think the most important thing at first is to keep it simple, seriously.<br /> <br /> You don't need to present every clan and bloodline, every power, every faction, position and political currents.<br /> <br /> Show them the Seven Clans and the basic gist of being a Vampire. From there, everything else is optional. Of course you'll answer their questions if something else picks their interest, but throwing everything up front will just overload them. Overloaded people don't make informed decisions, they make panicked decisions.<br /> <br /> Let the setting present itself in the game, and be open if at some point they want something they didn't knew about before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}